# Security & Pentest Testing Rules (5-Layer Safety Gate)

1. **Default-Deny Scope Guard:** All active DAST, fuzzing, and pentest scripts MUST validate `TARGET_BASE_URL` via `tools/security/pentest_scope_guard.py` (`PentestScopeGuard`) against `ALLOWED_PENTEST_HOSTS`. Never target production domains, cloud metadata (`169.254.169.254`), or sensitive infrastructure ports.
2. **Explicit Consent & Audit Trail:** Require `--confirm-pentest-scope` (or `PENTEST_CONSENT_ACKNOWLEDGED=1`) before dispatching active payloads, preserving tamper-evident logs in `.synapse/pentest_audit.log`.
3. **Rate-Limit & Circuit Breaker:** Cap active probing to `<= 10 req/s` and `<= 5` concurrent workers with `timeout <= 10s`, aborting automatically on consecutive `5xx`/`429` responses.
4. **Non-Destructive PoC & Account Isolation:** Use benign read-only probes only (zero `DROP`/`TRUNCATE`/unscoped `DELETE`). Verify BOLA/IDOR strictly across isolated test account pairs (`PENTEST_USER_A`, `PENTEST_USER_B`).
5. **Credential Hygiene & Evidence Redaction:** Load auth tokens exclusively from environment variables and redact all JWTs, cookies, API keys, and PAN/PII in exported reports.
